From: KOReader <https://github.com/koreader/koreader-base>
Subject: [PATCH] willuslib: keep the Win32 code paths' callees out of `#if 0`

Upstream's `4c11f61 disable some unused code` wrapped several runs of
libk2pdfopt in `#if 0`. Two of those runs contain functions that Windows does
need: MinGW defines `WIN32`, `willus.h` turns that into `HAVE_WIN32_API`, and
code guarded by it calls them.

  * `wsys_win32_api()`, called from `wfile.c`'s `wfile_findfirst`,
    `wfile_findnext` and `wfile_findclose`:

        undefined reference to `wsys_win32_api'

  * `wfile_increment_hour()` and `wfile_decrement_hour()`, called from `win.c`'s
    `win_ntfs_date_to_proper_date()` and `win_proper_date_to_ntfs_date()`, plus
    the four helpers those two call among themselves (`wfile_increment_day`,
    `wfile_decrement_day`, `wfile_days_in_month`, `wfile_leap_year`):

        undefined reference to `wfile_increment_hour'

Neither shows up on the platforms upstream builds for, so neither was noticed.

Each fix closes the disabled run before the needed functions and reopens it
after, so everything else in those runs stays disabled exactly as upstream left
it. No-op elsewhere, where nothing calls them.

diff --git a/willuslib/wfile.c b/willuslib/wfile.c
index 695b971..477d5c4 100644
--- a/willuslib/wfile.c
+++ b/willuslib/wfile.c
@@ -811,6 +811,13 @@ int wfile_saved_during_daylight_savings(char *filename)
     }
 
 
+/* NOTE: `win.c` calls these from `win_ntfs_date_to_proper_date()` and
+ *       `win_proper_date_to_ntfs_date()`, and MinGW compiles win.c because
+ *       it defines `WIN32`. Keep them outside the block above, which upstream
+ *       closed around the rest of this run. These six call one another, so
+ *       they move together. */
+#endif
+
 void wfile_increment_hour(struct tm *ts)
 
     {
@@ -959,6 +966,8 @@ int wfile_leap_year(int year)
     return((year%400==0) || ((year%100!=0) && (year%4==0)));
     }
 
+#if 0
+
 #endif
 
 /*
diff --git a/willuslib/wsys.c b/willuslib/wsys.c
index f4d7762..5dae13c 100644
--- a/willuslib/wsys.c
+++ b/willuslib/wsys.c
@@ -245,6 +245,12 @@ static void gnu_compiler(char *compiler_version)
 #endif
 
 
+/* NOTE: MinGW defines `WIN32`, which `willus.h` turns into `HAVE_WIN32_API`,
+ *       and `wfile.c` then calls this from `wfile_findfirst`, `wfile_findnext`
+ *       and `wfile_findclose`. Keep it outside the block above, which upstream
+ *       closed around the rest of this run. */
+#endif
+
 int wsys_win32_api(void)
 
     {
@@ -261,6 +267,8 @@ int wsys_win32_api(void)
 #endif
     }
 
+#if 0
+
 
 /*
 ** Return the status of a process.
